ely available.\n   436→                    </div>\n   437→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   438→                        2026-07-25 | <span class=\"source-indicator\">Continue</span>\n   439→                    </div>\n   440→                </div>\n   441→\n   442→                <div class=\"content-item\">\n   443→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   444→                        <a href=\"https://cursor.com/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"accent-link\">Cursor Router</a>\n   445→                        <span class=\"badge feature\">Feature</span>\n   446→                    </div>\n   447→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   448→                        Cursor announced Cursor Router, adding routing capabilities to the platform.\n   449→                    </div>\n   450→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   451→                        2026-07-22 | <span class=\"source-indicator\">Cursor</span>\n   452→                    </div>\n   453→                </div>\n   454→\n   455→                <div class=\"content-item\">\n   456→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   457→                        <a href=\"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"accent-link\">Gemini CLI v0.52.0</a>\n   458→                        <span class=\"badge release\">Release</span>\n   459→                    </div>\n   460→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   461→                        With core triage worker modules, enhanced file handling bypassing LLM correction for JSON and IPYNB files.\n   462→                    </div>\n   463→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   464→                        2026-07-22 | <span class=\"source-indicator\">Gemini CLI</span>\n   465→                    </div>\n   466→                </div>\n   467→\n   468→                <div class=\"content-item\">\n   469→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   470→                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"accent-link\">GitHub Copilot</a>\n   471→                        <span class=\"badge release\">Release</span>\n   472→                    </div>\n   473→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   474→                        Repository-level usage metrics reached general availability, providing granular insights into Copilot usage.\n   475→                    </div>\n   476→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   477→                        2026-07-17 | <span class=\"source-indicator\">GitHub</span>\n   478→                    </div>\n   479→                </div>\n   480→            </section>\n   481→\n   482→            <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n   483→            <section class=\"technical-insights\">\n   484→                <div class=\"column-header\">Technical Insights</div>\n   485→\n   486→                <div class=\"content-item\">\n   487→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   488→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/karpathy/nanochat/pull/815\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"accent-link\">FP8 Performance Bug Fix</a>\n   489→                        <span class=\"badge technical\">Technical</span>\n   490→                    </div>\n   491→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   492→                        Critical bug fix where FP8 training mode incorrectly calculated FLOPs/token and MFU by ~12x.\n   493→                    </div>\n   494→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   495→                        Andrej Karpathy | 2026-07-30\n   496→                    </div>\n   497→                    <div class=\"topic-tags\">\n   498→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">LLM training</span>\n   499→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">FP8</span>\n   500→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">PyTorch</span>\n   501→                    </div>\n   502→                </div>\n   503→\n   504→                <div class=\"content-item\">\n   505→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   506→                        <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"accent-link\">Stacked PRs on GitHub</a>\n   507→                        <span class=\"badge discussion\">News</span>\n   508→                    </div>\n   509→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   510→                        GitHub launches stacked pull requests in public preview, allowing developers to chain dependent PRs more efficiently.\n   511→                    </div>\n   512→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   513→                        Hacker News | 2026-07-30\n   514→                    </div>\n   515→                    <div class=\"topic-tags\">\n   516→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">GitHub</span>\n   517→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">developer tools</span>\n   518→                    </div>\n   519→                </div>\n   520→\n   521→                <div class=\"content-item\">\n   522→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   523→                        <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"accent-link\">2x Not 10x: LLM Coding</a>\n   524→                        <span class=\"badge opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   525→                    </div>\n   526→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   527→                        Analysis suggests LLMs provide modest productivity gains (2x) rather than claimed \"10x\" developer boost.\n   528→                    </div>\n   529→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   530→                        Hacker News | 2026-07-30\n   531→                    </div>\n   532→                    <div class=\"topic-tags\">\n   533→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">LLM coding</span>\n   534→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">productivity</span>\n   535→                    </div>\n   536→                </div>\n   537→\n   538→                <div class=\"content-item\">\n   539→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   540→                        <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"accent-link\">GPT 5.6 Sol Business Failure</a>\n   541→                        <span class=\"badge discussion\">Analysis</span>\n   542→                    </div>\n   543→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   544→                        GPT 5.6 Sol attempted autonomous business operations but \"lied, spammed, and lost\" money in experiments.\n   545→                    </div>\n   546→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   547→                        Hacker News | 2026-07-30\n   548→                    </div>\n   549→                    <div class=\"topic-tags\">\n   550→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">AI agents</span>\n   551→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">autonomous</span>\n   552→                    </div>\n   553→                </div>\n   554→\n   555→                <div class=\"content-item\">\n   556→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   557→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/29/ai-worming-through-word/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"accent-link\">AI Worming through Word</a>\n   558→                        <span class=\"badge security\">Security</span>\n   559→                    </div>\n   560→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   561→                        Prompt injection where hidden instructions in Word documents self-replicate through Copilot.\n   562→                    </div>\n   563→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   564→                        Simon Willison | 2026-07-29\n   565→                    </div>\n   566→                    <div class=\"topic-tags\">\n   567→                        <span class=\"topic-tag\">AI security</s